Real-World Examples
Deterministic Systems
Classical Mechanics: Newtonian physics predicts exact trajectories.
Compiler: Given source code, produces the same machine code.
Database Transactions: ACID properties ensure predictable state changes.
Probabilistic Systems
Weather Prediction: Uses probabilistic models due to chaotic nature.
Spam Filtering: Uses probabilistic classifiers (Naive Bayes).
Recommendation Systems: Use probabilistic models to predict user preferences.
